                <pb facs="0865" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg777"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eddy to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-12-24"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Eddy reports that a note practically embodying all the points contained in
                    Department’s telegram of the 23d instant, but referring to the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arabia</hi> only, had already been presented to the
                    minister of foreign affairs, and that he will send another note to the foreign
                    office including all the vessels. Urges that all powers of attorney be
                    telegraphed without delay.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
